# Implement image placement and layering

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical status below describes implementation still unavailable after
this finite theoretical acceptance.

Expose source identity, crop, scale, opacity, z-order, below-text, inline,
above-text, and clipped-region placement without overwriting the original.

Current executable command evidence covers source identity on an existing
semantic figure. `AssetReference` can attach, replace, or remove a reference to
an asset already admitted in the same accepted revision, including nested
figures and atomic Undo. The value cannot carry raw bytes, base64, filesystem
paths, or remote URLs, so it does not implement media ingestion.

A transport-neutral placement intent now keeps that original source identity
separate from caller-owned crop, position, size, transform, opacity, z-order,
resolution policy, color handling, and placement constraints. Below-text,
inline, above-text, and clipped-region modes are explicit. Coordinate units,
transform/crop evaluation, opacity ranges, semantic figure integration, derived
line-art, decoding, rendering, and command transport remain open.

## Finite source-preserving image placement contract

**Inputs:** one already admitted immutable asset identity, its intrinsic pixel
size, one stable figure identity, accepted page revision/geometry, and caller-
authorized placement intent (mode, crop, size, position, opacity, z-order).
**Outputs:** a new typed placement constraint referencing the same original
asset, a preview proposal, or a refusal. No placement command may overwrite
original pixels, download a new URL or grant file/device authority.

**Modes:** `BelowText` permits painting behind the text layer; `Inline`
reserves measured flow space and may repaginate later content; `AboveText`
permits a foreground overlap subject to collision diagnostics; and
`ClippedRegion` restricts drawing to one explicitly measured page region.
All four modes retain exact source asset identity. Switching modes invalidates
the appropriate layout/diagnostic projections but does not change the asset.

**Worked example:** asset `photo-1` has intrinsic size `1200 x 800` pixels,
figure `f2` at revision `r4` references it. A typed edit sets a crop from
`(100,50)` through `(1100,750)` in source pixels, paper position `(25,40)` mm,
rendered size `50 x 35` mm, opacity `0.75`, and z-order `2`. The same saved
crop/size can be proposed in each of the four modes while keeping
`source_identity=photo-1`; the preview records any flow or collision changes.
A later crop adjustment must be reversible without changing original bytes.

**Geometry/admission rule:** crop coordinates are finite integer pixels with
nonempty dimensions wholly inside the asset. Position and size are physical
page units; size must be positive and any constrained placement must fit the
selected writable region or return a typed blocking diagnostic. Opacity
belongs to the closed range `0..1` and layer ordering is stable within each
explicit placement mode. Rendering must use only the admitted source and
never derive a replacement through a hidden font/image provider.

**Refusal example:** a crop ending at source x=`1300`, opacity `1.5`, missing
`photo-1`, stale `r4`, unsupported WebP decode, or physical output requesting
color photography must refuse with exact cause and retain the old placement.
There is no silent downsampling, automatic line-art conversion, or hidden
crop to make an incompatible live plan appear possible.

**Assumptions and limits:** semantic asset references and all four placement
intent variants are existing isolated domain primitives. Coordinate binding,
asset decoding, crop/transform evaluation, actual interactive editing,
rendering, line-art policy, and output-capability integration are unfinished.
This finite contract does not imply the preview currently supports the modes.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for source references and typed mode vocabulary;
  theoretical for crop/placement rendering and revision coordination,
  2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** immutable source invariant, four modes, physical/source
  units, one worked placement and invalid-crop/capability refusals.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** real editable placements, image
  ingestion, opacity rendering, transform evaluation, or live-plan output.
